  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Begin Defining Project Scope**\n\nOkay, I\'m starting to get a grip on the task. I need to build a website based on some images I don\'t have, but I\'ll use the HTML context as a guide. The style is strictly monochrome, high-contrast, gamer-tech festival, which I\'ll focus on when translating the images to code. I\'ll need to use Orbitron, Oxanium, and Inter fonts.\n\n\n**Refining UI Framework Elements**\n\nOkay, I\'ve got the design system nailed down now. I\'m focusing on the colors, fonts, and defined border parameters. I\'m now making a list of the specific UI components, like the Navbar, Hero Section, and Events Section. My job is to translate these specifications into concrete React components using the provided framework.\n\n\n**Focusing on Target Structure**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the file structure. Since I don\'t see any images, and the prompt asks me to build a website using the \"images above\", I\'m going to start with a Landing Page, incorporating elements from the provided HTML snapshots in the chat history. The primary entry point will be `src/App.tsx`, and I\'ll break down the Landing Page into sub-components.\n\n\n**Clarifying File Structure**\n\nI\'m now changing direction and focusing on a modular file system. My earlier instinct to keep everything in one file for simplicity is incorrect - the instructions mandate breaking it down into distinct components. I will create `Navbar.tsx`, `Hero.tsx`, `Countdown.tsx`, `EventSection.tsx`, and `EventCard.tsx` files. I also need to configure Tailwind with CSS variables.\n\n\n**Finalizing Component Assembly**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `Footer.tsx` component and updating `src/App.tsx` to integrate all the modular pieces. I\'m ensuring everything is correctly assembled and rendering as expected. I need to get this basic structure correct before moving on. I\'m focusing on making sure there are no rendering conflicts.\n\nI\'m now editing `src/index.css` to import the specified fonts and include the theme variables from the design system. I will start testing components in the browser, to ensure the fonts and styles render as expected.\n\n\n**Defining Theme Details**\n\nI\'ve set up the CSS variables for the color palette, establishing the foundation for the monochrome, high-contrast style. I\'ve defined shades for borders, text, and accents, which I\'ll implement throughout the website. Now, I will begin implementing the specified font weights and colors throughout the codebase. The `body` background is set to the base color, and the primary text color is white.\n\nI\'m now structuring the content and styling of each component. I have the `Navbar` with logo, links, and icons. Next, I have a `Hero` section with the \"SPECTRUM 26\" title and a `Countdown` component. Then, the `EventSection` features a title with an icon and grid-based `EventCard` elements.\n\n\n**Implementing File Structure**\n\nI am now creating the specific files, as instructed, and defining simple anchor links for a single-page scroll, while also integrating dummy routes. I am also planning to use lucide-react for the icons and CSS transitions to keep the code efficient. I will only output tool calls as requested.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Efficient Workflow**\n\nI\'m now determining how to proceed most efficiently. I\'ll focus on parallel `create_file` calls for component files to minimize overhead. I\'m focusing on writing the necessary CSS first, especially custom text sizes for Tailwind. After that, I will define a structure that uses the existing elements. I will create `Navbar.tsx`, `Hero.tsx`, `Events.tsx`, and `Footer.tsx` in individual files.\n\n\n**Refining Font Implementation**\n\nI\'m now incorporating the fonts from Google Fonts directly into `src/index.css` using `@import`. I\'ve defined CSS variables for the color palette, fonts, and theme-related values. I have the base styles established for the `body` element, including background and text colors. I\'m focusing on text-related utilities like text-hero, to improve efficiency.\n\n\n**Defining Text Style Classes**\n\nI\'m now creating text-related utility classes for Tailwind to streamline font styling. I\'ve defined font families, sizes (using clamp for responsiveness), weights, and line heights for hero titles, countdown text, section headings, card titles, regular headings, buttons, and body text. These utilities will ensure consistency throughout the site.\n\n\n\n**Refining Utility Class Syntax**\n\nI\'m now revising the Tailwind utility class definitions. Realizing my error, I\'ve corrected the `@utility` syntax, to ensure compatibility. I\'m focusing on text styling classes, which need adjustment for the v3 syntax of the framework. I will update the code with the correct syntax to accurately style elements.\n\n\n**Implementing Navbar Functionality**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `Navbar` component, adding the functionality. I\'m focusing on the navigation links and dark mode toggle, along with the user icon. I\'ve incorporated anchor links for smooth scrolling within the single-page structure and ensuring that the dark mode toggle responds correctly to user interactions. I\'m testing the navbar\'s responsiveness.\n\n\n**Constructing Hero Content**\n\nI am now focusing on the `Hero` section content. I\'m building it, using `SPECTRUM 26`, and a description. I\'m incorporating the `Countdown` component and updating the file to reflect these design decisions, ensuring it is correctly integrated into the overall layout. This is followed by visual formatting, applying the design specs.\n\n\n**Refining Countdown Component**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `Countdown` component and integrating it into the `Hero` section. I\'m focusing on rendering the time units (days, hours, minutes, seconds) correctly, ensuring that the visual styling matches the provided monochrome, high-contrast theme. I am now styling the components to reflect those specifications.\n\n\n**Defining Event Cards**\n\nI\'m now creating the `EventCard` components, focusing on integrating event data. I\'m taking the provided event data, then dynamically displaying the title, description, category, and image. I\'m ensuring each card displays correctly within the `EventSection`, applying the monochrome style, and testing their layout in the browser.\n\n\n\n**Implementing Event Display**\n\nI\'m now creating the `EventSection` to display the events, focusing on organizing the layout with grid components, which include two different types of events. I am creating two different event groups: a tech event group and a non-tech event group, each with different icons and border styles. I will now integrate the event data to dynamically render the event cards.\n\n\n**Integrating Event Cards**\n\nI am now completing the `EventSection` by integrating the two distinct groups of events, each with their associated styles, including the tech and non-tech events. I am also implementing the logic to dynamically render the `EventCard` components. I\'m focusing on ensuring each card displays correctly within its respective section, with the proper styles. I will now integrate the event data to render the cards in their appropriate grids.\n\n\n**Finalizing Card Styling**\n\nI\'m now completing the `EventCard` component and I\'ve focused on styling them to ensure they visually match the high-contrast aesthetic. I\'ve been applying the border styles dynamically. Also, I\'ve adjusted the hover states for interactivity. I am now creating the logic to correctly render them and implement them.\n\n\n**Finalizing Footer Integration**\n\nI am now implementing the `Footer` component, focusing on the content and structure, including the privacy, terms, and contact links, ensuring they are correctly styled. I\'m verifying the responsiveness and positioning of the footer elements. I\'m finishing integration of the footer into the main application layout and the complete site structure.\n\n\n**Confirming Deployment Structure**\n\nI\'m now integrating all the components, refining the application structure, and reviewing CSS variable use. I\'m focusing on ensuring proper nesting and inheritance of styles, and using the `App.tsx` and the `Footer.tsx` code snippets to verify that all the component integration is correct. I am verifying the deployment structure and dependencies, ensuring that all pieces fit together.\n\n\n**Refining Class Implementation**\n\nI\'m now implementing utility classes in Tailwind for consistent and efficient styling across the site. I\'ve defined new classes, to streamline text styling, ensuring consistent application across the various components. I\'m focusing on text styling classes, which need adjustment for the v3 syntax of the framework.\n\n\n**Refining Style Definitions**\n\nI\'m now integrating new text utility classes into the Tailwind setup. These are for hero titles, headings, buttons, body text, and small text. I\'ve also added a glow effect for stylistic highlights. I\'m making sure these utility classes are correct.\n\n\n"
