ables in CSS, covering background, border, and text colors, along with font families. I\'ve set up base, elevated, and card background colors, various border styles, and primary, secondary, and muted text colors. These are being implemented using CSS variables, ensuring easy modification.\n\n\n**Defining Text Styling**\n\nI\'m now defining text styles for the design. I\'m focusing on setting up utility classes for various text elements like hero text (large, bold, uppercase), card titles (uppercase), headings (bold), buttons (monospace, uppercase, letter-spacing), body text, small text, and micro text. Each utility is tailored for its specific role, with adjustments for font size, weight, and line-height. I\'m focusing on ensuring consistency.\n\n\n\n**Adjusting Component Styles**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how the newly defined text styles and color utilities can be applied to existing components, specifically looking at `Hero.tsx`, `Navbar.tsx`, and `Events.tsx`. I will adjust the `Navbar` to align with the new text styles, and update colors. I need to replace or consolidate redundant Tailwind classes.\n\n\n**Modifying CSS Utilities**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how to adjust the button styles to align better with the new theme using CSS utilities. I will create more CSS utilities to ensure consistency with button styles, especially for primary and secondary variants. I\'m noting the need to manage dashed and non-dashed states, and considering using `edit_file` to modify `index.css` directly. I will define utilities to consolidate the styles for button variations.\n\n\n**Refining Variable Application**\n\nI\'m now integrating `--color-` variables for background, border, and text. I\'ve defined new styles with these variables, with appropriate opacity values. These values are applied for `body` in `index.css`. Next, I\'m setting font families and sizing text with new `text-` utility classes to better match the theme\'s design language. I\'m focusing on ensuring styles sca