  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing UI Alignment**\n\nI\'m working to align the UI with the original prompt\'s visuals. I\'m focusing on the \"Bold Typography\" theme instructions now. Currently, I\'m extracting styling elements such as colors, fonts, spacing, borders, shadows, and gradients. Additionally, I am identifying layout patterns, especially concerning flexbox. My aim is to faithfully apply these extracted design elements.\n\n\n**Clarifying Design Intent**\n\nI realized my mistake. I misinterpreted the \"Design HTML\" as a complete replacement, not a style guide. The user explicitly wanted the existing app structure preserved. Now, I understand I need to extract the styling elements from the provided HTML and apply them to the existing components, without altering their structure or functionality. I am on the right track again and understand the requirements now.\n\n\n**Reconciling Visual Expectations**\n\nI\'m now focused on reconciling the current UI with the original, unretrieved image references. The user\'s feedback, \"not the same as the images,\" indicates a visual mismatch. I\'m carefully reviewing the existing components and styling, specifically the extracted CSS variables to see what is missing in the design. I need to deduce styling that is not in the CSS variables to match with the user\'s intent. The truncated context adds complexity, but I\'ll meticulously compare and contrast. I am confident I can discern the missing elements.\n\n\n**Investigating Hero Component**\n\nI\'m now diving into the Hero component, specifically `src/components/Hero.tsx`. My current focus is on understanding its layout and comparing it against the mental image I have of the \"images\" the user mentioned. I\'m looking at the component structure and considering how it might be altered to better reflect the desired visual. I am looking for inconsistencies in the current implementation.\n\n\n**Examining Font Application**\n\nI\'ve discovered a critical discrepancy. I replaced the